WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.728
One wrong number can spoil a whole report.

2
00:00:03.728 --> 00:00:08.851
In this lesson, you will learn to replace wrong values, round numbers the way

3
00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:12.876
you need, and use the Information tools to test your numbers.

4
00:00:12.876 --> 00:00:14.340
Let's fix some data!

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.373
Here is the Units Sold column in the Financial Sample table.

6
00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:25.305
Some values have decimals, like two thousand one hundred eighty three point five.

7
00:00:25.305 --> 00:00:28.720
Units should be whole numbers, so let's fix that.

8
00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:46.862
First, Replace Values.

9
00:00:46.862 --> 00:00:50.348
Right click a value, or use the Transform tab.

10
00:00:50.348 --> 00:00:53.447
In Value To Find, type the wrong value.

11
00:00:53.447 --> 00:00:57.320
In Replace With, type the correct one. Then click OK.

12
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.789
Each replacement becomes a new step:

13
00:01:12.789 --> 00:01:15.575
Replaced Value, Replaced Value one, and so on.

14
00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.360
You can click any step to check it.

15
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.437
Now, Rounding.

16
00:01:28.437 --> 00:01:30.648
On the Transform tab, open Rounding.

17
00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:33.596
Round Up goes to the next whole number.

18
00:01:33.596 --> 00:01:36.175
Round Down goes to the one before.

19
00:01:36.175 --> 00:01:39.860
And Round lets you choose the number of decimal places.

20
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.836
I choose Round, with zero decimals.

21
00:01:57.836 --> 00:02:01.040
In the formula bar, you see Number dot Round.

22
00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.600
Every value in Units Sold is now a whole number.

23
00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.532
Next to Rounding is Information.

24
00:02:09.532 --> 00:02:12.830
Is Even returns true or false for each value.

25
00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:19.060
You also have Is Odd and Sign, which tells you if a number is positive or negative.

26
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.804
But Is Even replaced our numbers with true and false!

27
00:02:28.804 --> 00:02:33.460
That is not what we want here, so I delete that step in Applied Steps.

28
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.496
The Standard menu is right beside it, with Add, Multiply, Divide, and more.

29
00:02:52.496 --> 00:02:57.660
Practice each tool, and always check the result before you move on. Well done!

